DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The yyddss driver supports Yamaha DS-XG based sound chips, as found in,
     e.g., many Sony Vaio notebooks.

     The flags can be used to pass additional information to the yyddss driver.

     A value of 0x1000 forces the driver to disable the Sound Blaster legacy
     mode.  This is needed to make the floppy work on some machines but is
     disabled by default because it is known to break apm(4) support.

FFIILLEESS
     The driver needs a firmware file, which is loaded on demand when the de‐
     vice is attached:

           /etc/firmware/yds

